  "details": "## Issue\n\nThere's no way to switch platforms and upload an avatar with one click instead of 2.\n\n## Benefit\n\nThis should save a lot of time because we aren't always checking if the platform has switched as those usually takes 3 to 20 minutes so we usually forget about.\n\n## Intended behaviour:\n\n1. Switch platform to Android (from windows)\n\n2. When prompted if we want to confirm the switch also ask if we want to upload the avatar to the new target platform.\n\n3. If we decided to push the \"Upload\" button it should do a \"Build and Publish\".\n\n4. The avatar that will be decided to upload will be the one that was marked in the multi-platform build or more precisely the \"VRC Per Platform override\" \n\n## Notes\n\nThe new prompt window will be one with 3 buttons instead of 2, those being:\n\n1. Switch\n\n2. Upload\n\n3. Cancel\n\n## Technical\n\nIn the VRCSdkControlPanelBuilder.cs\n\nLine 2521 to 2571 is the code for the window prompt in the avatar SDK.\n\n## Screenshot related\n\nFirst image is the original window prompt and the other is a concept for the new window.\n\nThe text could be modified a little as to reflect what \"Upload\" will do.",
